==Swedish==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|sv}} {{m|non|þorp}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|sv}} {{m|gem-pro|*þurpą}}, whence also with German {{m|de|Dorf}} and Dutch {{m|nl|dorp}}.

===Noun===
{{sv-noun|n}}

# {{lb|sv|before 16th century}} A solitary [[farm]], distant from other settlements
# {{lb|sv|16th century}} ''Officially defined'' as a very small farm
# {{lb|sv|17th century to early 20th century}} A small farm, [[rent]]ed from a larger [[land owner]], where the rent was payed through work on the owner's land ([[dagsverken]])
# {{lb|sv|after the 1940's}} A small [[cottage]] in the [[countryside]]

